 "differential_reads": "Exactly the three labels are added and nothing is removed; the other ten filings' D02 candidates are byte-identical and all twelve D03 sets are unchanged.",
 "question": "Which blocks inside Item 3 and the notes a filing incorporates does D02 leave out, and what would reading italic as a heading mark add?",
 "record_type": "ISSUE_47_D02_ITALIC_NOTE_LABELS",
 "what_this_does_not_do": "It does not make either Paramount value acceptable: both still hold a block the _LEGAL keyword proxy admits from outside the incorporated note (2025: blocks 2108 and 2257; FY2024: block 2010), which is a registered defect with its own decision.",
 "why_they_were_dropped": "Paramount sets its category captions in bold italic ('Claims Related to Former Businesses') and the matter labels under them in italic alone. The inherited _substantive needs twelve characters; historical_text_results._note_heading admitted a shorter block inside an incorporated note only when it was bold or underlined."
